  "subtitle": "The repair tool you plugged into a dead computer's brain socket",
  "why_scout_cares": "The 9010A is the only artifact in the museum where the human physically swaps their instrument INTO the dead machine's CPU socket and becomes the processor. A field-repair HCI with a beeping keypad, a probe that flashes red and green, and ROM signatures you look up in a table by hand. It is also the arcade repairman's sacred tool — the thing that debugged Pac-Man and Defender PCBs — which ties it directly to the museum's arcade exhibits.",
  "search_terms": ["Fluke 9010A", "micro-system troubleshooter", "signature analysis", "interface pod", "arcade repair"],
